      "score": 0.816,
      "text": "Defects in autophagy have been observed in multiple models of neurodegenerative disease, including Alzheimer\u2019s, Huntington\u2019s, and amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS; Rubinsztein et al., 2005; Ventruti and Cuervo, 2007; Mari\u00f1o et al., 2011). However, the biogenesis, maturation, and dynamics of autophagosomes in neurons are only poorly understood. Most studies to date have focused on model systems that lack the extended and highly polarized processes that characterize neurons (Jahreiss et al., 2008; Kimura et al., 2008)."
