      "score": 0.796,
      "text": "We find that autophagosome dynamics remain robust in a mouse model of neurodegenerative disease, but autophagosome flux is not increased even as protein aggregates accumulate along the axon. Thus, in primary neurons, the dynamics of the autophagy pathway are robust and spatially specific but may not be efficiently up-regulated in response to increased protein aggregation."
